Solve the game by direct reasoning from observations, notes, and lightweight tool use. Keep durable hypotheses in `notes/actor_beliefs.md`, but do not spend effort building a persistent simulator or planner for the game.

When the mechanics or objective are uncertain, choose actions that either make progress or distinguish competing hypotheses. Some cells may be HUD or interface state (budgets, lives, timers, selected tools, progress indicators, validation lights, status bars); treat them as observations of game state, not decoration, and infer their role from transitions and terminal evidence.
